  "allowedDifferences": [
    "tools/list is an MCP-protocol capability; the direct transport is an in-process adapter and has no tool registry. Not a Tier-1 document semantic.",
    "direct `help` is a client-side stub ({success:true,verb:\"help\"}); the CLI grammar reference is served by the legacy transport. Vocabulary parity is asserted separately (legacy help lists every adapter verb); help does not mutate documents.",
    "direct `help <topic>` is a client-side stub; grammar discovery goes through the legacy transport. No document mutation involved.",
    "flush wrapper wording/timing differs (direct closes the resident handle; legacy may auto-flush first). Persistence is proven by the persisted-view case below.",
    "0-slide pptx screenshot: resident pipe rejects grid rendering with no pages ('--page 1 out of range (total slides: 0)') while the CLI one-shot path the MCP tool uses renders a blank grid. Tier-1 semantics unaffected: no gate-mandated flow screenshots a 0-slide deck (create is baseline-exempt; final screenshots follow writes), validation/persistence/edits all agree, and non-empty deck screenshots agree (pptx-baseline-shot / pptx-final-shot). An existing 0-slide .pptx is a degenerate artifact not producible by PowerPoint.",
    "error wrapper differs by transport (direct: adapter `command_failed` envelope; legacy: CLI `Error: Path not found…` text). Same semantic category: CLI rejected the selector; no document mutation (verified below).",
    "direct rejects a missing path client-side (PipiUI containment, code path_rejected); legacy defers to the CLI (File not found). Same semantic category: missing-file rejection, no document touched.",
    "direct enforces the frozen verb vocabulary client-side (unknown_verb); legacy prints CLI help with isError=true. Same semantic category: unknown verb never reaches a document.",
    "PipiUI client-side lexer policy (unterminated quote) — frozen in command-gate-parity/direct-adapter tests; the raw MCP server is not required to duplicate PipiUI policy."
  ],
  "fixes": [
    "adapter toBatchItem: add/add-part now map the parent positional to `parent` (was `path`; the resident defaults a missing parent to /body, which made pptx slide/shape adds impossible and silently retargeted docx adds)",
    "adapter runSdk: view screenshot mode now requests the JSON envelope (the resident returns the rendered PNG path only in JSON mode for pptx; text mode returned an empty Stdout)"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Screenshot comparison: qualification + successful valid-PNG render on both transports (never bytes). Dimensions are recorded per transport as delivery metadata: direct writes the native grid contact sheet to a temp PNG; legacy MCP inlines a downscaled render.",
    "Persistence: explicit flush (save/close) then re-open `view <file> text` through each transport plus on-disk zip checks in both roots.",
    "Raw wrapper text, process/PIDs, timing and absolute temp roots are allowed differences; roots are scrubbed to <ROOT> in this evidence.",
    "Edit echo: transports agree on the mutation-outcome line; the CLI one-shot may append decoration lines (e.g. default geometry for an added shape) that the resident envelope omits. Persisted content is compared exactly via persisted-view."
  ]
}
